// A console port (component D20's terminal half, M3's virtio-console): a
// stream of bytes to and from someone at the other end, as every console
// port driver provides it.

/// A console port: a byte stream between this machine and whoever is at
/// the other end (a virtual machine's host, a serial line's terminal).
///
/// Bytes that arrive travel through a ring in a frame the client shares
/// (`connect`), as an input device's events do: a record is 8 bytes, the
/// number of bytes it carries (1 to 7) then the bytes, and the client's
/// notification is signalled when records were added and the client said
/// it sleeps (the `silica_ring` rule). The ring holds 256 records; what
/// arrives while it is full, or before a client connects beyond 4 KiB, is
/// dropped. Bytes are the other end's, unchecked: text or not, the client
/// decides.
///
/// One client is connected at a time; a new `connect` replaces the old one.
protocol silica.console.Port version 1 {
    /// Why a call was refused.
    enum Error : u32 {
        /// The frame is not a frame of 4 KiB the driver may write.
        bad_memory = 1,
        /// The other end did not take the bytes in time.
        stalled = 2,
    }
    /// Start receiving: `ring` is a frame of 4 KiB for the ring, `arrived`
    /// is signalled when records were added and the client sleeps.
    connect @1 (ring: cap<Frame>, arrived: cap<Notification>) -> () error Error;
    /// Send `data` (at most 2048 bytes a call); answered once the device
    /// has taken it.
    write @2 (data: bytes) -> () error Error;
}
